Subject: [BACKPORT] Keep Cam Link polling policy local to that device

The Cam Link Pro probe must not write the global irq_service parameter.
Otherwise later MK.2/4K Pro probes lose MSI even if the Cam Link probe
fails loading firmware. Preserve explicit irq_service=0 and MSI fallback.
GPL-2.0-or-later; based on sc0710 PR #89 pin 5564ede7fb88.

diff --git a/lib/sc0710-core.c b/lib/sc0710-core.c
index 8ed8210..7ab75c8 100644
--- a/lib/sc0710-core.c
+++ b/lib/sc0710-core.c
@@ -1035,9 +1035,7 @@ static int sc0710_initdev(struct pci_dev *pci_dev,
 		 * the small-descriptor conveyor redesign lands. */
 		printk(KERN_INFO "%s: Cam Link Pro: using polling DMA service\n",
 			dev->name);
-		irq_service = 0;
-	}
-	if (irq_service) {
+	} else if (irq_service) {
 		if (pci_alloc_irq_vectors(pci_dev, 1, 1, PCI_IRQ_MSI) == 1 &&
 		    pci_request_irq(pci_dev, 0, sc0710_irq, NULL, dev,
 				    "%s", dev->name) == 0) {
